        "prompt": "$(3x+7y)^2-(2x-3y)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x+10y)(5x+4y)$\n\nApply the difference of two squares to the complete brackets.",
          "worked": "Using $A^2-B^2=(A-B)(A+B)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(3x+7y)^2-(2x-3y)^2&=(3x+7y-2x+3y)(3x+7y+2x-3y)\\\\(3x+7y)^2-(2x-3y)^2&=(x+10y)(5x+4y)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p37-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(5x+2y)^2-(3x-y)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(8x+y)(2x+3y)$\n\nApply the difference of two squares to the complete brackets.",
          "worked": "Using $A^2-B^2=(A-B)(A+B)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(5x+2y)^2-(3x-y)^2&=(5x+2y-3x+y)(5x+2y+3x-y)\\\\(5x+2y)^2-(3x-y)^2&=(2x+3y)(8x+y)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
